From ceb7e1839f82ab9cc895d6b4f65d95918d874bc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@y.z>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:40:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/21] aarch64: boot console on a device tree
 simple-framebuffer

Without a GOP (stock ABL / U-Boot DT handoff) the panel stayed blank
until vesad. Right after the early serial console, take the DT
simple-framebuffer if check_placement() accepts it against the kernel's
boot data, the bootloader's free areas and the DT carve-outs; write it
through the bootloader's PHYS_OFFSET identity map, register exactly the
visible buffer as Reserved so memory::init maps it write-combining and
keeps it out of the allocator and physmap, and stop per-write cache
cleaning once that mapping is live. The DT record wins over a GOP
framebuffer, as it does in vesad; a mismatch is logged.

Co-Authored-By: Cursor <noreply@cursor.com>
